186: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL187: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL188: 【78†era-boojum-cuda】  | 【78†era-boojum-cuda】  |    |\nL189: 【79†era-boojum】  | 【79†era-boojum】  |    |\nL190: 【80†era-cuda】  | 【80†era-cuda】  |    |\nL191: 【81†plonky2-crypto】  | 【81†plonky2-crypto】  |    |\nL192: 【82†plonky2-ecdsa】  | 【82†plonky2-ecdsa】  |    |\nL193: 【83†plonky2-examples】  | 【83†plonky2-examples】  |    |\nL194: 【84†plonky2-gpu-bench】  | 【84†plonky2-gpu-bench】  |    |\nL195: 【85†plonky2-sha256】  | 【85†plonky2-sha256】  |    |\nL196: 【86†plonky2-sha512】  | 【86†plonky2-sha512】  |    |\nL197: 【87†plonky2】  | 【87†plonky2】  |    |\nL198: 【88†plonky2_ed25519】  | 【88†plonky2_ed25519】  |    |\nL199: 【89†plonky2_sha512】  | 【89†plonky2_sha512】  |    |\nL200: 【90†proto-neural-zkp】  | 【90†proto-neural-zkp】  |    |\nL201: 【91†.gitignore】  | 【91†.gitignore】  |    |\nL202: 【92†Cargo.lock】  | 【92†Cargo.lock】  |    |\nL203: 【93†Cargo.toml】  | 【93†Cargo.toml】  |    |\nL204: 【94†LICENSE】  | 【94†LICENSE】  |    |\nL205: 【95†LICENSE-APACHE】  | 【95†LICENSE-APACHE】  |    |\nL206: 【96†LICENSE-MIT】  | 【96†LICENSE-MIT】  |    |\nL207: 【97†NOTICE】  | 【97†NOTICE】  |    |\nL208: 【98†README.md】  | 【98†README.md】  |    |\nL209: 【99†rust-toolchain.toml】  | 【99†rust-toolchain.toml】  |    |\nL210: [Button: View all files]\nL211: ## Repository files navigation\nL212: \nL213:   *   * 【100†README】\nL214:   * 【100†License】\nL215:   * 【100†Apache-2.0 license】\nL216:   * 【100†MIT license】\nL217: \nL218: More items\nL219: # MegaZK (open-source)\nL220: \nL221: GPU-accelerated Plonky2 proving.\nL222: This repository is the open-source implementation of MegaZK, the system described in the ICS '26 paper 【101†MegaZK: A Memory Efficient GPU System Accelerating End-to-end Zero-Knowledge Proof†dl.acm.org】 (DOI: 【102†10.1145/3797905.3807842†doi.org】). Citation: Muyang Li, Yueteng Yu, Bangyan Wang, Xiong Fan, Mingyu Gao, and Shuwen Deng. 2026. In Proceedings of the 40th ACM International Conference on Supercomputing (ICS '26). ACM, 1165–1176. 【102†https://doi.org/10.1145/3797905.3807842†doi.org】\nL223: The GPU proving path lives in the forked 【103†`plonky2`】 crate and calls into 【104†`era-boojum-cuda`】 / 【105†`era-cuda`】 for CUDA kernels and runtime bindings.\nL224: \nL225: The default Cargo feature set is CPU-only and does not build CUDA dependencies. In the benchmark programs, `--baseline` selects the CPU prover; the GPU path is opt-in with `--features gpu`. Running a non-baseline benchmark without that feature returns `GPU proving is unavailable; rebuild with --features gpu`.\nL226: This monorepo is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. See 【94†`LICENSE`】 and 【97†`NOTICE`】.\nL227: ## Repository Layout\nL228:   * 【103†`plonky2`】: forked Plonky2 workspace. GPU proving enters through `build_gpu` / `GpuCircuitData::prove` and the `plonky2/plonky2/src/integration` module.\nL229:   * 【104†`era-boojum-cuda`】: CUDA kernels and Rust wrappers used by the GPU prover.\nL230:   * 【105†`era-cuda`】: CUDA runtime bindings.\nL231:   * 【106†`plonky2-sha256`】, 【107†`plonky2-sha512`】, 【108†`plonky2-examples`】, 【109†`proto-neural-zkp`】: benchmark applications.\nL232:   * 【110†`plonky2_ed25519`】: experimental Ed25519 benchmark. Proof generation is expected to run, but verification currently has a known issue (`BENCHMARK_VERIFY_STATUS: KNOWN_ISSUE`). That is not a regression.\nL233:   * 【111†`plonky2-gpu-bench`】: std-only internal helper for shared benchmark timing, verification policy, and CUDA memory reporting.\nL234: ## Current Reproduction Environment\nL235: \nL236: The following environment is the current known reproduction baseline. Other versions may work, but have not been normalized for this open-source snapshot.\nL237:   * OS: Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS, Linux 6.8.0-124-generic, x86_64\nL238:   * Rust: `nightly-2023-11-28` (pinned in 【99†`rust-toolchain.toml`】)\nL239:     * `rustc 1.76.0-nightly (49b3924bd 2023-11-27)`\nL240:     * `cargo 1.76.0-nightly (9b13310ca 2023-11-24)`\nL241:   * CUDA toolkit: 12.x (this snapshot was built with 12.5, `nvcc V12.5.82`)\nL242:   * CMake: 3.30.3\nL243:   * clang: 14.0.0\nL244:   * GPU/driver: requires an NVIDIA GPU and driver compatible with CUDA 12.x. If CMake cannot detect the GPU architecture during build, set `CUDAARCHS` manually, for example `CUDAARCHS=89`.\nL245: The repository has a pinned toolchain in 【99†`rust-toolchain.toml`】. For CPU baseline comparisons, `RUSTFLAGS=-Ctarget-cpu=native` can improve performance on the local machine.\nL246: ## Support Matrix\nL247: \nL248: Benchmark  | GPU proof  | CPU baseline  | Verification status\nL249: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL250: Factorial  | Supported  | Supported  | Expected to pass\nL251: Fibonacci  | Supported  | Supported  | Expected to pass\nL252: SHA256  | Supported  | Supported  | Expected to pass\nL253: SHA512  | Supported  | Supported  | Expected to pass\nL254: ECDSA  | Supported  | Supported  | Expected to pass\nL255: MVM  | Supported  | Supported  | Expected to pass\nL256: Ed25519  | Experimental  | Experimental  | Known verification issue\nL257: Ed25519: prove is expected to run; verify is a known failure (`KNOWN_ISSUE`), not a regression.\nL258: ## Benchmark Circuit Sources\nL259: \nL260: These are the open-source circuit / gadget implementations used by each benchmark (not the proving-system libraries). Commands below are this repository's CLI; full smoke and paper-scale invocations are in 【112†Build And Run】. Paper numbers in brackets are ICS '26 camera-ready references. No pinned commit is recorded in this snapshot, so links go to the upstream repository root.\nL261:   * Factorial — run: `-p plonky2 --example factorial` (for example `-- --num 2000`). Circuit: 【113†0xPolygonZero/plonky2】 (paper [27]; in-tree 【114†`plonky2/plonky2/examples/factorial.rs`】).\nL262:   * Fibonacci — run: `-p plonky2 --example fibonacci` (for example `-- --num 2000`). Circuit: 【113†0xPolygonZero/plonky2】 (paper [27]; in-tree 【115†`plonky2/plonky2/examples/fibonacci.rs`】).\nL263:   * SHA256 — run: `-p plonky2_sha256` (for example `-- --num 1`). Circuit: 【116†polymerdao/plonky2-sha256】 (paper [30]; in-tree 【106†`plonky2-sha256/`】).\nL264:   * SHA512 — run: `-p plonky2_sha512` (for example `-- --num 1`). Circuit: 【117†polymerdao/plonky2-sha512】 (paper [31]; in-tree 【107†`plonky2-sha512/`】).\nL265:   * ECDSA — run: `-p plonky2-examples --example 4_ecdsa_verification` (for example `-- --num 1`). Circuit example: 【118†qope/plonky2-examples】 (paper [36]; in-tree 【108†`plonky2-examples/`】). ECDSA gadget used by that example: 【119†0xPolygonZero/plonky2-ecdsa】 (in-tree 【120†`plonky2-ecdsa/`】).\nL266:   * Ed25519 — run: `-p plonky2_ed25519` (for example `-- --num 1`). Circuit vendored in this tree: 【121†Electron-Labs/plonky2_ed25519】 (in-tree 【110†`plonky2_ed25519/`】). Paper [29] cites 【122†polymerdao/plonky2-ed25519】; the files here match Electron-Labs (authors, `curve25519-dalek` git rev, and layout), not the polymerdao tree.\nL267:   * MVM — run: `-p neural-zkp --bin rust-app` (for example `-- --input-size 100 --output-size 100`). Circuit: 【123†worldcoin/proto-neural-zkp】 (paper [43]; in-tree 【109†`proto-neural-zkp/`】). The vendored `Cargo.toml` still lists `https://github.com/dcbuild3r/proto-neural-zkp/` as `repository`; that is a contributor copy of the Worldcoin project.\nL268: ## Build And Run\nL269: \nL270: Run the following commands from the repository root.\nL271: \nL272: The default feature set is CPU-only. Use `--features gpu` for the GPU prover, and `--baseline` for the CPU prover in the benchmark CLIs.\nL273: \nL274: This is a root Cargo workspace. Commands below use `--locked` so they build from the checked-in root `Cargo.lock`. rustup will pick `nightly-2023-11-28` from 【99†`rust-toolchain.toml`】. GPU builds need CUDA 12.x, an NVIDIA driver, and (when CMake cannot detect the architecture) `CUDAARCHS`.\nL275: The commands in this README are this repository's CLI.\nL276: Every benchmark reports `Time taken to build:`, `Time taken to prove:`, and `Time taken to verify:` using Rust `Duration` formatting. GPU runs also report used and free CUDA memory with a shared format. MVM retains its existing seven-column CSV output in addition to these human-readable timings. A completed verification also emits exactly one `BENCHMARK_VERIFY_STATUS: PASS`, `BENCHMARK_VERIFY_STATUS: KNOWN_ISSUE`, or `BENCHMARK_VERIFY_STATUS: FAIL` machine-readable status line.\nL277: ### Smoke (small workloads)\nL278: \nL279: #### Factorial\nL280: \nL281:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2 --features gpu --example factorial -- --num 2000\nL282:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2 --example factorial -- --num 2000 --baseline\nL283: \nL284: #### Fibonacci\nL285: \nL286:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2 --features gpu --example fibonacci -- --num 2000\nL287:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2 --example fibonacci -- --num 2000 --baseline\nL288: #### SHA256\nL289: \nL290:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2_sha256 --features gpu -- --num 1\nL291:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2_sha256 -- --num 1 --baseline\nL292: \nL293: #### SHA512\nL294: \nL295:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2_sha512 --features gpu -- --num 1\nL296:     cargo run --locked --release -p plonky2_sha512 -- --num 1 --baseline\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn7view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xuezhantong/zk-debloater/main/LICENSE\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xuezhantong/zk-debloater/main/LICENSE: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn7view3 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/main/LICENSE\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://raw.githubusercontent.com/THU-HAS/MegaZK/main/LICENSE: Cache miss"
